 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf impute [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [--chromosomes CHROMOSOMES]\n                             [--min-gp MIN_GP] [--min-info MIN_INFO]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Genotype-only VCF (e.g. chip calls) to impute with Beagle instead.\n  --chromosomes CHROMOSOMES\n                        Chromosomes, e.g. chr20 or chr1-22 (default: every installed one).\n  --min-gp MIN_GP       Minimum max GP (default: GLIMPSE2 0.9; Beagle 0.95).\n  --min-info MIN_INFO   Opt-in INFO/DR2 site filter; meaningful only for multi-sample cohorts.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf impute --input lowpass.bam --chromosomes chr20\n  wgsextract vcf impute --vcf-input chip.vcf.gz\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  imputed.vcf.gz (+ .tbi): every imputed record marked INFO/IMP, low-\n  confidence ones FILTERed ImpLowConf.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, bgzip, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also:\n  GLIMPSE2_ligate, GLIMPSE2_phase; hours on a 30x genome.\n",
